event('c:finite-super-criterion','independent re-proof','Read the complete written theorem. Schematic super-orbit ideal, finite stable generators, projective lifting after one fixed P0, signed polynomial polarization, rectangular SFT for all mixed tensors, and trace cancellation using any external algebraic parity lift all pass. No Chow-idempotent parity lift or Kimura assumption is used. Minor regular-representation wording corrected by Part C.')
event('c:finite-super-criterion','targeted proof check','Checked root proposed extension to any characteristic-zero Weil coefficient field K: I_Q=ker(O(W_Q)->O(G_Q) tensor K) is a rational G_Q-stable ideal; vanishing rational covariants have precisely coordinates in I_Q. All finite-cover and positive parity-trace arguments remain rational. Only finite existence is asserted without effective coefficient arithmetic; no rational Betti structure is presumed.')
event('C.1.minimal-rectangle-Kimura','used and rechecked in this run','Opened original Del Padrone-Mazza2005 Theorem2.1 full proof, Proposition3.1 and Theorem3.2 p286. Under C+(X), the exact minimal rectangle is equivalent to Kimura finiteness and nilpotence on every power, for any Weil cohomology. This is a consequence of condition(ii), not an additional premise. Arbitrary Schur-finiteness and the faithful-realization Andre-Kahn theorem are explicitly distinguished.')
event('thm:B-Brauer-characteristic','independent re-proof','Independently verified the proposed F2 constant elliptic example y^2+y=x^3: direct formal-group calculation gives kerF=alpha2; constant A1 sections make F2[t]/F2[t^2] inject into H1(S,E)[2]. The section splits Rf*Gm and truncated derived cohomology embeds these actual order-two classes disjointly from all base classes. Full quotient infinite; prime-to-characteristic finiteness not refuted. Detailed b3_full_brauer_supersingular_audit.md.')
