event('c:hyperkahler-chow-unramified','first proof','Opened Ito-Zou2026 complete Lemmas4.2-4.3 and Theorem4.4 proof: all-degree WD purity holds over the original local field, not only after extension. Tensor stability discharges the ambient-purity premise in the Saito/Chow-projector reduction for homogeneous rational Chow summands of hyper-Kahler products, yielding original-base unramifiedness independence. Scoped fragment sent Part C; arbitrary nonalgebraic projectors are not upgraded.')
event('C.6.Ito-Zou-scope','source gate checked','Read complete Proposition5.7, Theorem5.8 and Corollary5.10 with surrounding hypotheses. Strong G-valued compatibility requires connected monodromy and a semistable Kuga-Satake variety over the chosen base; general local Frobenius compatibility is only after finite extension, except b2=3. No false descent of unramifiedness through a ramified extension is inferred.')
event('thm:B-relative-surface-gate','independent re-proof','Read the entire written sections/b3_surface_gate.tex after independently checking both directions. Tate-divisor surjectivity plus HS and the pure-weight1 geometric Leray quotient gives rational Brauer surjectivity and finite cokernel. Pencil with extending section gives injection of surface Brauer; restriction-corestriction descends finiteness even if ell divides extension degree. Constant-field and cohomological-Brauer scopes pass. Exact Kahn6/8 and Morrow4.3 sources independently opened. Detailed b3_surface_gate_independent_audit.md.')
event('B.2.Scholbach-ordinary-Hom','targeted proof check','Checked Part B finite-supported object counterexample mathematically: Hom_DM(Z)(1,i_*1[1])=H_M^1(Fp,Q0)=K_-1(Fp)_Q=0, whereas continuous ell-adic H1(Fp,Qell)=Qell for ell not p. Ordinary motivic Hom cannot equal the full Weil-absolute theory on that category. Did not independently reopen Scholbach axioms in this check; generic conditional f-cohomology comparison remains separate.')
