event('prop:B-diagonal-Chow-gate','independent re-proof','Read complete b1_diagonal_gate.tex and primary Balkan-Schreieder Corollary1.3, Theorem7.1(2), Remark7.2 and section7.4. The upper-half reduction uses affine cohomological dimension; t=d-2i+1 sends (d,i) to (2m-1,m), m=d-i+1, and pushforward splits the projective-product map. No Chow hard Lefschetz or threefold-only universal reduction is asserted. Detailed b1_b2_final_independent_audit.md.')
event('def:B-corrected-comparison-package','targeted proof check','Read complete b2_comparison_package.tex. Enhanced global category and functorial arithmetic comparison are stated as a conjectural package; local f/g conditions, dual completion, real correction and localization are retained. The finite-field and Tate-specialization checks do not claim existence of the global package.')
event('prop:B-comparison-specializations','independent re-proof','Checked finite-field Weil cone and extension-degree normalization, and the number-ring Tate specializations with dual completion against the written package. Finite-field assertion retains all stated Geisser hypotheses; unconditional Tate graded spaces do not establish the conjectural global category or every gluing map.')
event('prop:B-Scholbach-finite-support','used and rechecked in this run','After the earlier mathematical-only check, independently read archived Scholbach Axiom1.1, Definitions1.3 and1.7, Axiom1.8 and Remark6.2. The category contains i_*1, ordinary Hom gives K_-1(Fp)_Q=0, while continuous H1(Fp,Qell)=Qell. This refutes the full ordinary-Hom identification, not the conditional generic f-cohomology comparison.')
event('thm:B-relative-surface-gate','targeted proof check','Checked proposed equivalent single group H3(F0 P3_Fpbar,Qell(2))^GammaFp=0 against Balkan-Schreieder Theorem7.1(1), Remark7.2, Proposition4.6 and Notation4.8. Section2.1 defines variety as integral, not geometrically integral. A smooth projective variety over a finite constant extension remains an integral smooth projective Fp-variety; induced cohomology and Shapiro identify its invariants with those over the constant field. The prime-field group therefore has exactly the required all-constant-fields quantifier.')
