event('B.3.all-bases-surface-gate','independent re-proof','Read complete pending_b3_all_bases_surface_gate.md. Proper alteration descent of invariant Kummer classes passes: the degree-one restriction kernel is E2^(1,0), pure weight minus1; rational section equalizers descend by graph image, Frobenius and Verschiebung; singular double intersections use the existing Kummer injection. Nilpotent and finite-open-cover extensions retain all bases. This gate was already counted in CP04; audit preserved in b3_all_bases_integral_audit.md.')
event('B.3.integral-torsor-lattice','first proof','Under surface Tate, proved H1(S,A) tensor Z_(ell) finitely generated for every finite-type Fp base and abelian scheme. The proper-cover kernel maps to actual section Cech H1 with p-primary kernel; its localization is a submodule of a finite Lang-Neron lattice. Regular-cover H1 is torsion and has finite ell-part. Nilpotent and open-cover descent complete the proof. Full argument in b3_all_bases_integral_audit.md.')
event('B.3.proper-torsor-descent','targeted proof check','Handled proper algebraic-space torsors explicitly: the schematic graph image of a Cech-equal trivialization is proper quasi-finite, hence finite and a scheme; Kelly Corollary20 applies there. Frobenius supplies a section of P^(p^r), and Verschiebung supplies a section of [p^r]_*P. Therefore the actual Cech-kernel is p-primary; exact integer localization yields the claimed injection without an unproved etale-to-h comparison.')
event('B.3.regular-cover-torsion','used and rechecked in this run','Opened Stacks0AF8 Remark110.74.2 and Lemma110.74.3. The remark removes the dimension2 restriction and proves regular-noetherian generic-point injection for abelian torsors; the field lemma proves torsion for smooth commutative group algebraic spaces. Expanded the Picard trick using the extended line bundle homomorphism phi_L=0 and separatedness. Original Raynaud XIII.2.6 full text remains unobtained.')
event('B.3.singular-Picard-degree','first proof','The integral torsor lattice implies finite ell-primary H1(S,Pic_X/S) for every smooth proper geometrically connected curve under surface Tate, even with infinite period: quotient H1(S,J) by the finitely generated degree-obstruction subgroup; H1(S,Z) is torsion-free by surjectivity H0Z->H0Z/n.')
event('B.3.genus-one-base-image','scope gate checked','The remaining Brauer quotient step concerns torsion lifting from full H2(S,Gm)/delta Pic_rel(S). A nontorsion base class can become ell-torsion modulo that image; finite generation of the image alone does not bound its ell-saturation. Isolated genus-one infinite-period case after the nonzero-degree canonical-bundle cases. No saturation theorem or counterexample established; full H2Gm torsion shortcut excluded by opened singular examples.')
