event('c:finite-power-cutoff','independent re-proof','Read the actual added Gamma_m expansion and finite-power corollary. The adjoint of the unit-complement projector gives the signed nonempty-subset partial-diagonal formula, with trace(1)=0 for positive dimension. Pullback to a larger power splits by intersection with degree-one point classes and projection, preserving the narrow rings; the displayed maximum therefore suffices.')
event('c:recursive-elimination-bound','independent re-proof','Read all181 lines of the uniform-bound fragment. Controlled Dickson tree is finite by the proved nondecreasing-subsequence induction and finite branching; homogeneous pair degrees double at most; accepted leading monomials form a bad sequence. Dehomogenization uses h^e f^h membership and needs no saturation assumption. Detailed c1_uniform_arity_independent_audit.md.')
event('c:uniform-arity-bound','independent re-proof','Verified all even/odd variable counts, exterior-module generators, square-zero Y encoding, preservation of Y degree by homogeneous pair reduction, elimination intersection and conversion to input arity. Quadratic Y terms cannot contribute to the linear module part. No closed Dube bound or arbitrary mixed-super invariant exactness is used.')
event('c:uniform-arity-scope','targeted proof check','The uniform bound only on n,a,b requires a rational table. For presented coefficients every kappa-form coordinate must be a named generator, and coefficient variables are eliminated together with group variables to obtain the rational contraction. With that clarification max(q+3,e+1) is correct; no unspecified Weil-field arithmetic algorithm is asserted.')
event('lem:B-Gm-proper-kernel','independent re-proof','Read the full actual written kernel proof. Bhatt-Scholze Theorem4.1(ii) and Proposition4.5 at rank1 give R1 epsilon_*Gm=0 and only the needed H2_et-to-H2_v injection. Cech degree2 kernel has E_infty^(1,1) and E_infty^(2,0), bounded by Pic(T1)[1/p] and units(T2)[1/p]. The argument requires only a finite-type cover whose perfection is a v-cover, including affine-open covers followed by alterations.')
event('prop:B-singular-proper-Brauer-gate','independent re-proof','Read complete sections/b3_proper_brauer_descent.tex. Under surface Tate a smooth projective alteration has finite ell-Brauer; the finitely generated Cech kernel then gives finite generation of full H2(S,Gm) tensor Z_(ell) for proper S. The separate nonproper boundary warning was correct at this stage and is now resolved by the later unit-cup theorem.')
event('prop:B-integral-torsor-lattice','independent re-proof','Read complete sections/b3_integral_torsor_lattice.tex. Proper algebraic-space torsor graph image is finite and a scheme; Frobenius plus Verschiebung makes the actual Cech kernel p-primary. Exact integer localization injects it into the finite section-Cech lattice. Regular-cover torsion and the surface-Tate finite ell-part complete the integral H1 result; relative Picard degree quotient and torsion-free H1(Z) are handled without assuming positive degree.')
event('lem:B-unit-cup-generation','independent re-proof','Read the full written smooth unit-cup proof. Boundary divisor relations equal rational units because Pic0 over Fpbar is torsion; alteration trace and norm identify the weight0 part of H1(1), while weight minus1 contributes no arithmetic coinvariants. Tate-divisor plus HS and finite cotype gives finite cokernel. Initial scope is smooth quasi-projective to match Riou ample hypotheses. This check verifies the proof mathematics; root separately reopened Riou exact trace statements and degree proof.')
event('lem:B-unit-cup-kernel','first proof','Proved unconditional finite kernel for unit cyclic cups on every finite-type finite-field scheme. Generic normal projective models give an injective finite divisor matrix on the unit lattice; arithmetic residue characters multiply by finite constant-field degrees, preserving full column rank. Smith normal form gives finite kernel. Nonreduced units are bounded p-primary and arbitrary singular/nonseparated schemes are allowed.')
event('thm:B-all-bases-Brauer-units','first proof','Completed the arbitrary-base conditional theorem with root and Part B inputs. Smooth quasi-projective h-cover unit-cup cokernel, arbitrary-base unit-cup kernel, rational unit equalizer and finitely generated full-H2 cover kernel give a uniform LMN error. Modulo the divisible unit-cup image, the remaining map has finitely generated kernel and finite bounded-exponent image in a finite-cotype quotient. Thus full H2 tensor Z_(ell) modulo unit cups is finitely generated, exactly equivalent universally to surface divisor Tate.')
event('cor:B-all-bases-relative-Brauer','first proof','Equal global units imply equal cyclic-cup images, so the relative ell-primary Brauer cokernel is a quotient of the finite absolute Brauer group modulo unit cups. Smooth proper geometrically connected fibres give equality of units including nonreduced bases. This resolves the arbitrary singular, nonproper and nonseparated base-image obstruction and even applies in higher relative dimensions; the universal curve converse is the prior surface pencil argument.')
