event('B.3.prime-uniform-descent','first proof','Proved the all-prime-to-p abstract descent with R=Z[1/p], D=Q/Z[1/p]. Single integral valuation and unit-lattice matrices give finite defects uniformly; K is already finitely generated over R. Divisibility of q*C makes the h-torsion of Br(T)[p-prime]/q*C a quotient of finite Br(T)[h], replacing any unproved prime-uniform finite-cotype assertion. Full proof and independent smooth-source check preserved post05/b3_prime_uniform_independent_audit.md; typeset integration pending.')
