event('C.6.pure-local-encoding-constraints','first proof','Wrote two scoped method diagnostics in post08/pure_local_encoding_constraints.md. Hyperbolic doubling of a map of rankr gives balanced weight pieces of dimension s+t but N-rank2r, so the stated WM-purity requirement forces the original map to be an isomorphism. Kisin local constancy rules out a smooth projected lisse family through0 detecting x*a_l=0 for all rational x near0. Neither is a general geometric nonexistence theorem.')
